    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d799-a2">

                <pb facs="0660" n="544" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg544"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Justice Lamar to
                        Señor Rabasa.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Niagara Falls</hi>, N. Y.</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-06-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 18, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Rabasa</hi>: I have your letter June 17th
                    in reply to my letter of June 15th answering your objections to the American
                    plan.</p>
                <p>I agree with you that it is not advisable for us in this manner to continue the
                    discussion of subjects which are before the Mediators. I, however, avail myself
                    of this opportunity to say that the words “Provisional President” in the first
                    paragraph of my letter were obviously a clerical error—not only the immediate
                    context but the whole letter showing that the reference was to a “Permanent
                    President” to be elected by the people of Mexico and not to a “Provisional
                    President” selected through mediation.</p>
                <p>With renewed assurances of respect [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. R. Lamar</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
